ge** (`src/search/controller.ts` only, 5 lines added, 1 changed):\n- Each `search()` call takes a number from a `latestRequest` counter, including calls with an empty query.\n- After the API call settles, results, error and `loading: false` are applied only if that call is still the latest.\n- Clearing the query resets state immediately as before, and because it also bumps the counter, late responses can no longer repopulate results.\n\nThe public API, state shape and the API/view modules are untouched.\n\n**Verification:**\n- `npm test`: the 4 existing tests pass.\n- The existing tests don't cover overlapping requests, so I ran a temporary check with manually resolved requests, kept outside the repo and deleted afterwards. All four scenarios passed:\n  - A stale success is ignored and loading stays on.\n  - An older request finishing after a newer one is ignored.\n  - A stale error is ignored.\n  - Clearing while requests are in flight leaves state empty, with no further subscriber notifications.\n\nNo tests were modified, no dependencies installed, and nothing is committed.\n\nSuperseded HTTP requests are still left to finish and their responses discarded, not aborted. Aborting them would mean passing an `AbortSignal` through `SearchApi.search`, which changes the public interface, so I left it out.","ttft_ms":1425,"type":"result","duration_ms":22965,"uuid":"033a96e4-64ca-4107-8f2c-081388603a79","ttft_stream_ms":820,"time_to_request_ms":23,"first_content_frame_ms":820,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
